# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — Physical state contract for boj-server-cartridges
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: must.ncl
# Verb:          must
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements.
# Run with: must check
# Fix with: must fix (where a deterministic fix exists)
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-07. The previous version was rsr-template-repo's own
# Mustfile and contained checks that could not pass here:
#   * governance-docs required GOVERNANCE.adoc; commit c2da9ed removed it in
#     favour of GOVERNANCE.md
#   * template-readonly grepped .machine_readable/0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml; the
#     manifest lives at repo ROOT, and it carries no RSR_TEMPLATE_DO_NOT_EDIT
#     marker
#   * anchors-directory and self-validating-structure required directories
#     that have never existed in this repository
#   * no-placeholder-values grepped the whole contractiles/ directory for a
#     brace pair that the check line itself contained — it matched itself
#
# EVERY `run:` line below was executed against the working tree on 2026-08-07
# (commit 972cf0e) and exited 0. Keep it that way: a check that cannot pass is
# worse than no check, because it trains readers to ignore red.

[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"
verified-on-commit = "972cf0e"

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for boj-server-cartridges, the canonical registry
of BoJ capability cartridges. Hosts fetch from this repository on demand and
no longer bundle a fallback tree, so these are hard requirements: CI and
pre-commit hooks fail if any check fails.

Every check here is deterministic, dependency-free POSIX shell run from the
repository root. Checks that need a toolchain (deno, zig, idris2) live in
the CI workflows and in .machine_readable/6a2/PLAYBOOK.a2ml, not here.
@end

## File Presence

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist
- run: test -f LICENSE
- severity: critical

### readme-present
- description: README.adoc must exist
- run: test -f README.adoc
- severity: critical

### changelog-present
- description: CHANGELOG.md must exist (one of the sanctioned .md exceptions)
- run: test -f CHANGELOG.md
- severity: critical

### security-policy
- description: SECURITY.md must exist at root and in .github/
- run: test -f SECURITY.md && test -f .github/SECURITY.md
- severity: critical

### ai-manifest-at-root
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml lives at the repository ROOT, not under .machine_readable/
- run: test -f 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml && test ! -f .machine_readable/0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical
- notes: The previous Mustfile grepped .machine_readable/0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml, which does not exist. This check pins the correct location so the mistake cannot recur.

### governance-docs
- description: GOVERNANCE.md, MAINTAINERS.adoc and .github/CODEOWNERS must exist
- run: test -f GOVERNANCE.md && test -f MAINTAINERS.adoc && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical
- notes: GOVERNANCE is .md here, not .adoc. Commit c2da9ed removed the duplicate GOVERNANCE.adoc deliberately; do not "restore" it.

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable
- severity: critical

### toolchain-pins
- description: .tool-versions must exist and pin zig, deno and idris2
- run: test -f .tool-versions && grep -q '^zig ' .tool-versions && grep -q '^deno ' .tool-versions && grep -q '^idris2 ' .tool-versions
- severity: critical

### dev-shell
- description: flake.nix must exist (Nix fallback tier; there is no guix.scm here)
- run: test -f flake.nix
- severity: critical

## Directory Structure

### contractiles-complete
- description: All required contractile directories exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable/contractiles && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/bust && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/dust
- severity: critical

### contractiles-files-present
- description: All four primary contractile files exist
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Trustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Adjustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### bust-dust-files-present
- description: Bustfile and Dustfile exist in their directories
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### six-directory-present
- description: 6a2 directory exists with all six checkpoint files
- run: test -d .machine_readable/6a2 && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/META.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/PLAYBOOK.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/AGENTIC.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/NEUROSYM.a2ml
- severity: critical

## Registry Integrity

### schema-mirror-present
- description: The pinned schema mirror and its pinning record both exist
- run: test -f schemas/cartridge-v1.json && test -f schemas/PINNED-SHA
- severity: critical

### schema-mirror-sha
- description: schemas/cartridge-v1.json content SHA-256 matches schemas/PINNED-SHA
- run: test "$(sha256sum schemas/cartridge-v1.json | awk '{print $1}')" = "$(awk -F'"' '/content_sha256/ {print $2}' schemas/PINNED-SHA)"
- severity: critical
- notes: Same assertion the cartridge-schema workflow makes. A silent mirror bump must fail loudly. If you intend the bump, update PINNED-SHA in the same commit.

### manifests-exist
- description: At least one cartridge.json exists (guards against a vacuous pass on a bad checkout)
- run: test "$(find cartridges -name cartridge.json | wc -l)" -ge 1
- severity: critical
- notes: A registry with zero manifests is a broken checkout, not a clean one.

### taxonomy-placement
- description: Every cartridge.json sits directly under domains/<domain>/, cross-cutting/<category>/ or templates/ (ADR-001)
- run: test -z "$(find cartridges -name cartridge.json | grep -vE '^cartridges/(domains/[^/]+|cross-cutting/[^/]+|templates)/[^/]+/cartridge\.json$')"
- severity: critical

### validator-present
- description: The manifest validator that enforces the schema gate is in-tree
- run: test -f tools/validate-cartridges/main.ts && test -f tools/validate-cartridges/deno.json && test -f tools/validate-cartridges/main_test.ts
- severity: critical

### minting-template-present
- description: The canonical minting template exists with all five layers
- run: test -d cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/abi && test -d cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi && test -d cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/adapter && test -f cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/cartridge.json && test -f cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig
- severity: critical

### proof-gate-scripts-present
- description: Both proof-gate scripts referenced by .github/workflows/proofs.yml exist
- run: test -f scripts/check-trusted-base.sh && test -f scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh
- severity: critical

### tooling-present
- description: The minter and the Foundry wizard referenced by PLAYBOOK.a2ml exist
- run: test -f tools/cartridge-minter/mint.ts && test -f tools/foundry/foundry.sh
- severity: critical

## Reference Integrity

### 6a2-workflow-paths-resolve
- description: Every workflow path cited in a 6a2 file actually exists
- run: for p in $(grep -ho 'workflow = "[^"]*"' .machine_readable/6a2/*.a2ml | sed 's/.*"\(.*\)"/\1/'); do test -e "$p" || exit 1; done
- severity: critical
- notes: Added because AGENTIC.a2ml used to cite .machine_readable/bot_directives/, a path that has never existed in this repository.

### no-template-project-identity
- description: No 6a2 file claims to be a different project
- run: test "$(awk -F'"' '/^project = /{print $2}' .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml .machine_readable/6a2/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml .machine_readable/contractiles/*.a2ml | sort -u)" = "boj-server-cartridges"
- severity: critical
- notes: STATE.a2ml declared rsr-template-repo and ECOSYSTEM.a2ml declared pseudoscript until 2026-08-07.

### no-unsubstituted-placeholders
- description: No unsubstituted template placeholders in the other three contractiles
- run: test -z "$(grep -l 'PLACEHOLDER' .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml .machine_readable/contractiles/Trustfile.a2ml .machine_readable/contractiles/Adjustfile.a2ml 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical
- notes: Deliberately scoped to the three sibling files rather than the whole directory. A directory-wide grep would match this check's own text — which is exactly why the previous version of this check could never pass.

## Text Integrity

### no-v-zig-substitution-corruption
- description: No cartridge doc claims Zig is banned (regression guard for the v->zig find/replace)
- run: ! git grep -qE 'zig (banned|predecessor)' -- cartridges
- severity: critical
- notes: A global "v" -> "zig" replacement once rewrote the estate's V-lang ban notes into claims that Zig is banned, across ~140 READMEs, in a repo whose FFI and adapter layers are Zig. V (vlang.io) is the banned language; Zig is its replacement.

### no-phantom-sidelined-files
- description: No doc references a SIDELINED-*.v.adoc file, because none exists
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files 'cartridges/*SIDELINED*')" && ! git grep -q 'SIDELINED' -- cartridges
- severity: critical
- notes: 96 adapter READMEs documented SIDELINED-*.v.adoc rows for files that exist nowhere in this repository or its history. Rows removed 2026-08-07.

### no-v-sources
- description: No V-language sources anywhere (banned estate-wide 2026-04-10)
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files 'cartridges/**/*.v')"
- severity: critical
- notes: Scoped to cartridges/ on purpose. Coq theorem files also use .v; there are none here, but a repo-wide check would be wrong in principle.

## Git State

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: All contractile files are tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/ 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### signed-commits
- description: HEAD must carry a valid signature
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: critical
